Jack: That sounds great. But the weather can change fast up there.
Lucy: True. I checked the forecast, and it said it would stay dry until Sunday.
Jack: Good. Then we should bring warm coats. The nights get really cold.
Lucy: I was going to pack a small first aid kit too, in case someone gets hurt.
Jack: Smart idea. I''ll bring the tent and some food.
Lucy: Perfect. Let''s leave early on Saturday morning, before the crowds.
Jack: Agreed. This will be our best adventure yet!', 'Lucy 提议周末去山里露营;Jack 担心天气多变;Lucy 说天气预报称周日前不会下雨;两人决定带保暖外套,因为夜里很冷;Lucy 还打算带急救包以防受伤;Jack 负责帐篷和食物;两人约定周六一早趁人少出发。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where do Lucy and Jack want to go this weekend?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Camping in the mountains.","Diving in the sea.","Shopping in the city.","Cycling along a river."]},{"q":"What did the forecast say about the weather?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It would rain all weekend.","It would stay dry until Sunday.","It would snow heavily.","There would be a storm on Saturday."]},{"q":"Why do they decide to bring warm coats?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Because the nights get very cold.","Because it will be very sunny.","Because the tent is too small.","Because they have nothing else to wear."]},{"q":"What was Lucy going to pack in case of injury?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A camera.","A first aid kit.","Some books.","A pair of boots."]},{"q":"When do they plan to leave?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Late on Sunday night.","On Friday afternoon.","Early on Saturday morning.","Next month."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U5', 'fltrp');
It is the highest mountain in the world.
The best time to climb it is in April and May.
The temperature there can drop as low as minus sixty degrees.
The first climbers confirmed to reach the top did so in 1953.', '珠穆朗玛峰位于尼泊尔和中国的边界上;它是世界最高峰;最佳攀登时间是4月和5月;那里的气温可低至零下六十度;最早被证实登顶的登山者是在1953年完成的。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where does Qomolangma lie?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["In the middle of the ocean.","Inside a large city.","Far away from any country.","On the border between Nepal and China."]},{"q":"When is the best time to climb it?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["In April and May.","In December and January.","Every day of the year.","Only at night."]},{"q":"How cold can it get on the mountain?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["About zero degrees.","As low as minus sixty degrees.","A little below freezing.","It never gets cold there."]},{"q":"When were the first climbers confirmed to reach the top?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["In 1924.","In 2011.","In 1953.","Last year."]},{"q":"What does the passage mainly tell us?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["How to cook on a mountain.","The history of one climber''s life.","Why people enjoy the sea.","Some basic facts about Qomolangma."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Tom: We did it to raise money for children in need.
Host: That''s wonderful. How did you prepare for such a hard trip?
Tom: We practised a lot. If we weren''t studying, we were out on our bikes.
Host: What difficulties did you meet on the road?
Tom: We had to climb steep hills day after day, and we faced falling rocks too.
Host: And how did you feel when it was all over?
Tom: It was the best feeling in the world. We had an adventure and helped others.', '主持人问 Tom 为何骑行那么远;Tom 说是为有需要的孩子筹款;问他如何准备,Tom 说勤加练习,不学习时就骑车;路上的困难是日复一日爬陡坡、还有落石;结束时他感觉好极了,既冒了险又帮了人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why did Tom and his friends cycle so far?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To raise money for children in need.","To win a big race.","To sell their bikes.","To find a new job."]},{"q":"How did they prepare for the trip?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They did nothing special.","They practised a lot on their bikes.","They only read books about cycling.","They bought a car instead."]},{"q":"What was one difficulty they met?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Too much free time.","No roads at all.","Climbing steep hills every day.","The trip was far too easy."]},{"q":"What danger did they face on the road?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Wild seals.","Deep snow.","Heavy traffic only.","Falling rocks."]},{"q":"How did Tom feel when the trip ended?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It was the best feeling in the world.","He was sorry he had started.","He felt bored and tired of it.","He never wanted to ride again."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U5', 'fltrp');
He is often called the Father of Science Fiction.
In his stories, he described machines years before they were really made.
One famous book follows a journey deep under the sea.
Even today, millions of readers still enjoy his amazing adventures.', '儒勒·凡尔纳是生活在19世纪的法国作家;他常被称为''科幻小说之父'';在故事里,他在机器真正造出来之前数年就描写了它们;一部名著讲述了一段深海之旅;直到今天,数百万读者仍喜爱他精彩的冒险故事。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was Jules Verne''s job?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He was a ship''s captain.","He was a French writer.","He was a doctor.","He was a mountain guide."]},{"q":"What is Verne often called?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The King of Poems.","The Father of History.","The Father of Science Fiction.","The Master of Maps."]},{"q":"What did Verne do in his stories?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["He copied old fairy tales.","He wrote only about his own city.","He drew pictures instead of writing.","He described machines before they were made."]},{"q":"What does one famous book follow?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A journey deep under the sea.","A walk through a desert.","A flight to the moon.","A climb up a mountain."]},{"q":"How do readers feel about his books today?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["No one reads them now.","Millions still enjoy them.","They find them boring.","Only writers can understand them."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Guide: Of course. Would you prefer a wreck dive or a scenic dive?
Visitor: What''s the difference between them?
Guide: On a wreck dive, you visit an old ship that sank long ago.
Visitor: And the scenic dive?
Guide: You swim with the grey seals that live around the islands all year.
Visitor: That sounds lovely. Are the seals dangerous?
Guide: Not at all. The young ones are curious and will follow you about.', '游客想预订本周六的潜水团;向导问他要沉船潜水还是观光潜水;游客问两者区别;向导说沉船潜水去看一艘很久前沉没的旧船,观光潜水则和常年生活在群岛周围的灰海豹一起游;游客担心海豹危险,向导说一点也不,小海豹很好奇,会跟着人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the visitor want to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Buy a fishing boat.","Climb a mountain.","Book a diving tour for Saturday.","Return a broken helmet."]},{"q":"What can you see on a wreck dive?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A row of new houses.","A busy fish market.","A forest on land.","An old ship that sank long ago."]},{"q":"What do divers do on the scenic dive?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They swim with the grey seals.","They study old maps.","They collect shells to sell.","They rest on the beach."]},{"q":"How long do the seals live around the islands?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only in summer.","All year round.","Just for a week.","Only on Saturdays."]},{"q":"What does the guide say about the young seals?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They are very dangerous.","They quickly swim away.","They are curious and follow divers.","They never come near people."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Always learn some first aid, so you can help if someone is hurt.
Tell a friend where you are going and when you plan to come back.
Check the weather, and never set out if a storm is coming.
With good planning, even a hard trip can become a safe and happy one.', '出发去任何冒险之前给你一个小贴士:先学点急救,以便有人受伤时能帮忙;把你的去向和计划返回的时间告诉朋友;查看天气,有风暴来临时绝不出发;有了周密计划,再难的旅程也能变得安全又快乐。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only ship captains.","Only young children.","Only doctors.","Anyone going on an adventure."]},{"q":"Why should you learn some first aid?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To help if someone gets hurt.","To win a prize.","To save money on food.","To travel more cheaply."]},{"q":"What should you tell a friend?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["How much money you have.","Where you are going and when you will return.","Which books you like.","What you ate for breakfast."]},{"q":"When should you never set out?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["When the sun is shining.","When you feel happy.","When a storm is coming.","When you have a map."]},{"q":"What can good planning do, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Make the weather change.","Stop all adventures.","Make a trip more dangerous.","Make a hard trip safe and happy."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U5', 'fltrp');

